  "verbalization": "Chenodeoxycholic Acid (Chenodeoxycholic Acid) is implicated in the pathogenesis of Choledocholithiasis through a chain of indications that links it to Cholelithiasis and Cholecystolithiasis. The evidence suggests that Chenodeoxycholic Acid may act as a precursor or modulator in the formation of gallstones, which in turn can lead to Choledocholithiasis. This relationship is supported by the indication chain where Chenodeoxycholic Acid is associated with Cholelithiasis, which is further linked to Cholic Acid, and Cholic Acid is indicated to cause Choledocholithiasis. The presence of multiple paths with varying scores indicates a potential role of Chenodeoxycholic Acid in the development of gallstone-related complications, particularly in the bile duct. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Chenodeoxycholic Acid contributes to the formation of gallstones and, subsequently, to Choledocholithiasis, emphasizing its role in the progression of gallstone disease.",
